"""Legacy D6 snapshot-mutant ELF builder (`snapshot-link --stubs zero`), plus `--stock` forwarding.

NOTE: The shipped `.GeneratedLean/cli-elf/libsignal-cli.elf` (pinned in `CliElf.lean`) is built
with stock LLVM `ld.lld` via `scripts/cli-elf-stock --stdbin` (or `scripts/cli-elf --stock ...`).
Snapshot mode below (`cli-elf/inputs.lock`) is retained solely for D6 bug-injection mutants.

Modes:
  scripts/cli-elf --build [--out-dir DIR] [--engine DIR] [--no-strip-runtime-debug]
                  [--image-dir DIR --crate-root DIR]
      Build `.GeneratedLean/cli-elf/libsignal-cli.elf` (and `link.json`) from source via engine
      `snapshot-link` (`StdBin` `--main-rust` + `rdl_shim.S` + `self-contained/libc.a`), verifying
      all pinned toolchain versions and input SHA-256 digests in
      `third_party/libsignal/libsignal-session/cli-elf/inputs.lock` and running the B2/F3
      branch-stub + zero-stub, `.img.text == code.bin` (on all non-branch words),
      dynamic `cli/io` placed-manifest (`SignalSessionIoIndex.json` + `SignalSessionIoPlacedObj`),
      and 0-reachable-`memcmp` verification. With `--image-dir` and `--crate-root` (plus an
      explicit `--out-dir` != `.GeneratedLean/cli-elf`, bug injection only): link the
      objects of `--crate-root`'s `libsignal-session` copy and verify against `--image-dir`'s
      `rust-obj2lean` export while enforcing all other `inputs.lock` pins and F3 checks.

  scripts/cli-elf --verify-pin [--elf PATH] [--lean-mod PATH] [--lock-only]
      Out-of-Lean SHA-256 check: fail-closed check against `inputs.lock` (and, unless
      `--lock-only` is passed, the single `sha256 "<64 lowercase hex>"` pin line in
      `LibsignalBinary/Specifications/SignalSession/CliElf.lean`).

  scripts/cli-elf --verify-io-manifest
      Out-of-Lean check of `.GeneratedLean/GeneratedLean/SignalSessionIo{Index.json,PlacedObj.lean,PlacedObj.bin}`
      against `inputs.lock` (5 blocks = 1,412 B, dynamic extern list from generated artifacts with
      0 hand-written extern names, `handle_error` crate-hash match against `img0`, and
      `__rust_no_alloc_shim_is_unstable_v2` resolution consistency per GK row 178).

  scripts/cli-elf --check [--elf PATH] [--engine DIR] [--no-strip-runtime-debug] [--cold-zig-cache]
      Determinism & embedding check: rebuild a second copy from source in a fresh workdir at a
      different path depth (optionally with an empty isolated `ZIG_GLOBAL_CACHE_DIR` /
      `ZIG_LOCAL_CACHE_DIR`), verify `.img.text` + branch stubs + zero stubs + dynamic
      `cli/io` placed manifest + 0 reachable `memcmp` stub references, and require `cmp` byte
      identity (0 differing bytes).

  scripts/cli-elf --self-test-alias-guard [--elf PATH]
      Run positive + negative self-tests for the GK row 185 (`A1–A7` + SR `S1–S5`) `check_std_elf`
      Block-621 `MergeFunctions` alias wrapper on isolated scratch copies.

Disclosure (GK rows 183 & 185, SR S1–S5):
  `snapshot-link/src/verify.rs::check_std_elf` (l.845–859) scans `.symtab` substrings (`"gimli"`,
  `"_Unwind_Backtrace"`, `"sigaltstack"`) as a name proxy for unwind/backtrace code. Under
  `rustc 1.98.1`'s LLVM `MergeFunctions`, exactly one pinned mangled symbol
  (`PINNED_STD_MERGEFUNC_ALIAS`, `<RawVec<gimli::read::unit::AttributeValue<..., usize>>>::grow_one`)
  is emitted as a zero-overhead `.symtab` `STT_FUNC` alias at `+0x0` of `PINNED_STD_MERGEFUNC_PRIMARY`
  (`<RawVec<Vec<u8>>>::grow_one`, `0x48837c`, `104` B), with `0` gimli/unwind bytes in the binary.
  Its `104` B body is Block `621` (`libsignalSessionPlacedCode621`) covered by
  `CliElfCodeMatchesPlaced` (`libsignalSessionMultiLib`), and no other forbidden name is accepted.
  Accepted until engine fix B (`verify.rs:845`) lands at M3, after which this wrapper branch is
  deleted (paired with a matching `DEVIATIONS.md` / `TRUSTED_BASE.md` disclosure in the `142(c)` PR).

Storage rule (`COMMON_BRIEF` §1): temporary work directories are created strictly under
`${XDG_CACHE_HOME:-$HOME/.cache}/cli-elf-tmp` (never `/tmp`) and cleaned up on exit.
"""
